doc Bitwise-and assignment: x &= y, short for x = x & y.
  ```
  let flags = 13
  flags &= 6
  print flags       // 4
  ```

  The left side can be any place of type `int`: a variable, a field, a
  slice element or `*p`, evaluated once.

needs std/let std/addr std/deref std/assign std/band
syntax statement
  {x: place int} &= {y: expr int}
expand
  let {$p} = &{x}
  *{$p} = *{$p} & {y}
